#!/bin/sh
# Start the window server and the desktop. They are SIBLINGS, not parent and child.
#
# gemd does NOT spawn the desktop. It must never know what a desktop is -- to gemd the
# desktop is just a client that happens to ask for a screen-sized, chromeless, bottom-most
# window (RESPONSIBILITIES.md §2, §4). The moment gemd launches it, gemd has a policy about
# desktops baked in, and "the desktop is just an app" stops being true.
#
# So both start here and they race. That is fine and deliberate: the desktop's connect to
# the "gem" service RETRIES until gemd is listening (gem_connect_set_wait). Whoever comes
# up second simply waits; neither has to be told about the other.
#
# It also means the desktop can be killed and restarted at will without touching gemd --
# exactly the property §4 promises, and why a restarted desktop comes back UNDERNEATH the
# apps that outlived it rather than on top of them.
#
# (This script lived ONLY on the SD card for a while, so the repo could not keep it
# correct: after a rename the card happily kept launching a stale binary. It is in-tree now
# and `make sdstage` owns it. Do not "fix" it by editing the card.)
/OS/bin/gemd &
/OS/bin/desktop &
